From adf4f10830151bb1ebbb57070e55e99836a6eb64 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:36:21 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 16/51] port: packed4 HWcc record layout (paper's 4 B record),
 owner key in the NR replica; release a failed install once

MEGALON_WMETA_LAYOUT=artifact64 (default, upstream 64 B line per record) | packed4 (-DWMETA_PACKED4):
WriteMetadata is the 32-bit sequence only (active_node had no reader; BlockId was read by reclaim only).
With DYN_WMETA the owner key moves to each node's NR replica (feature wmeta-rev): a reverse map
wmeta_idx -> key kept in dispatch_mut by diffing the touched keys, and a log op SwitchToReadOnlyByWmeta
that resolves the victim's key at its log position, so a stale key can never return another record.
The five reclaim sites use it under WMETA_PACKED4. Layout hash includes WMETA_PACKED4.

Also (both layouts): GCD_SLOT_WMETA_UPDATE_FAILED no longer recycles the record before falling through
to the second recycle (double decrement of the allocated count, or freeing another thread's reservation).

Rust tests: scr wmeta-rev 11/11, wmeta-rev 11/11, scr 8/8, none 8/8. Verifier: PASS-with-corrections.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
